From 6fc06b1227a991860ed609ff0d19c32dd630280f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:21:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] RISC OS: sound fed from any running thread, log at
 info, finer frame waits

SDL's audio thread is not used. CAudioBase opens SDL_mixer with
Mix_OpenAudioExternal and riscos/riscos_sound.cpp gives SharedSoundBuffer
23 ms blocks, keeping about 190 ms queued. The queue is topped up by the
frame loop (every frame and between the limiter's waits), the loading loop,
the client's and server's pack handling, the TBB stand-in's parallel_for
(a blocked_range now runs in up to 16 pieces, the hook between them) and a
feeding thread. riscos_progress.h declares the hook (weak).

The default log level is info (trace wrote about 170 lines a second). The
frame limiter waits a centisecond at a time (longer SDL_Delays rounded up,
giving 20-25 fps for 30). The presenter's figures and the sound feeding go
to the VCMI$Log file.
